# publish.manifest — the whitelist IS the structure contract: a listed item
# that is missing on disk hard-fails the export (and lint O1 catches it early).
# List only paths that exist NOW; add rows as features land.
# Paths are mirrored as-is into the export (no renames) — write your public
# README against the mirrored layout. Never whitelist a dir that contains an
# entry file (CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md): whitelist its code subtrees instead.
# Grammar, one directive per line:
#   target /tmp/{{name}}-export  # absolute; keeps a persistent .git → continuous public history
#   dir src                      # shipped whole (standard excludes applied)
#   file package.json            # shipped exactly
#   optional CHANGELOG.md        # shipped if present, no failure if absent
#   never RESEARCH.md            # extra internal name (or path) the guardrails must not find
#   allow-ref CLAUDE.md          # recorded exception: this built-in name MAY be
#                                # mentioned in shipped content (guardrail C)
readme README.public.md          # hand-kept public README, copied to README.md —
                                 # the internal README can never ship
